{
  "plugin": "basketball-scoreboard",
  "_comment": "Basketball keeps one manager per league and mode as a plain attribute -- nba_live, ncaam_recent and so on -- and only builds them when that league's enabled flag is set. Every mode's display() returns early unless games_list is populated, and the live path also reads live_games and active_celebration. display_mode picks which of the twelve screens is drawn. The card reads home_logo_path/away_logo_path off the game dict as Path objects, and period_text is what basketball.py's extractor builds (Q1-Q4, OT1, HALF, Final, Final/OT). Tournament shots additionally set is_tournament, away_seed/home_seed, tournament_round and tournament_region, and force march_madness.tournament_mode because the plugin otherwise decides from the calendar. Teams, scores and records are invented. The tournament round and region replace the 'Next Game' header, so they draw on the UPCOMING card only; seeds draw wherever records would.",
  "defaults": {
    "width": 128,
    "height": 32,
    "scale": 6,
    "freeze_time": "2026-03-21T23:30:00+00:00",
    "skip_update": true,
    "config": {
      "enabled": true,
      "nba": {
        "enabled": true
      },
      "wnba": {
        "enabled": false
      },
      "ncaam": {
        "enabled": false
      },
      "ncaaw": {
        "enabled": false
      }
    }
  },
